BT 1 0 0 1 0 120.3 Tm /F3 7.2 Tf 8.5 TL 1.6128 Tw (GymTrack is an Android application that supports gym members through the main) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.47608 Tw (stages of a workout routine: initial profile setup, workout-plan creation, exercise) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.085891 Tw (scheduling, live workout execution, and progress review. It is implemented in Kotlin) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.1796 Tw (with Jetpack Compose and uses a shared Room database to persist member profiles,) Tj T* 0 Tw .47736 Tw (workout plans and days, planned exercises, workout sessions, performed exercises, and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.325455 Tw (set records. The Home screen presents member information and recent activity. The) Tj T* 0 Tw .5298 Tw (Workout Schedule module lets users create and edit plans containing training days and) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.415927 Tw (exercises. During an active session, users can record repetitions and weights for) Tj T* 0 Tw .364985 Tw (individual sets, mark sets complete, control the workout timer, and finish or discard the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.7504 Tw (session. The Statistics screen derives summaries from completed database sessions,) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.148 Tw (including session count, completed sets and repetitions, training volume, duration,) Tj T* 0 Tw .507927 Tw (weekly activity, frequently trained exercises, and the heaviest recorded set. The project) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.3426 Tw (uses feature-oriented MVVM, repositories, Kotlin Coroutines, Flow, and Room) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.0176 Tw (transactions. This paper documents the implemented application, its architecture, data) Tj T* 0 Tw (model, user workflow, and current scope.) Tj T* ET
